From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:01:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix core error paths introduced by CIX ACPI support

Unpublish a pin controller when claiming its hogs fails. Reinitialize its
list node so that both the legacy registration failure and a later
unregister after register-and-init can release it safely.

Preserve regulator lookups without a consumer device, and initialize the
firmware protection-limit presence accumulator explicitly. The latter is
source hardening; the tested kernel already initializes automatic storage
to zero.

Signed-off-by: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/core.c b/drivers/pinctrl/core.c
index 2676f47..584a6a8 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/core.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/core.c
@@ -2266,8 +2266,12 @@ int pinctrl_enable(struct pinctrl_dev *pctldev)
 	mutex_unlock(&pinctrldev_list_mutex);
 
 	error = pinctrl_claim_hogs(pctldev);
-	if (error)
+	if (error) {
+		mutex_lock(&pinctrldev_list_mutex);
+		list_del_init(&pctldev->node);
+		mutex_unlock(&pinctrldev_list_mutex);
 		return error;
+	}
 
 	pinctrl_init_device_debugfs(pctldev);
 
diff --git a/drivers/regulator/core.c b/drivers/regulator/core.c
index baaf9bc..18f8f42 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/core.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/core.c
@@ -2201,7 +2201,7 @@ static struct regulator_dev *regulator_dev_lookup(struct device *dev,
 	regulator_supply_alias(&dev, &supply);
 
 	/* first do a dt based lookup */
-	if (has_acpi_companion(dev)) {
+	if (dev && has_acpi_companion(dev)) {
 		fwnode = fwnode_get_regulator(dev, supply);
 		if (fwnode) {
 			r = fwnode_find_regulator_by_node(fwnode);
diff --git a/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c
index da809a0..3553928 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ static void fwnode_get_regulator_prot_limits(struct fwnode_handle *np,
 	/* Protection limits: */
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(props); i++) {
 		char prop[255];
-		bool found;
+		bool found = false;
 		int j;
 		static const char *const lvl[] = {
 			"protection", "error", "warn"
